    "body": "**Judgement calls for the maintainer** (gate green, no golden changed, no column-engine verdict changed):\n1. **Sideways slack:** a column is cleared if it is within `tol` (0.01 mm) of the lowest part top within `tol` of its centre. The issue suggested `gate_tol(DEV_TOL, cell)` (0.066 mm), which would excuse cuts into the wall six times the stated tolerance. Real wall cuts of 12 µm, 50 µm and 1 mm still refuse in both engines.\n2. **Rest:** left unchanged; only the gouge side gets the slack.\n3. **The heavy lane `stock_engine_agreement` fails 2 tests on main** with the same output before and after this change, so the failure was already there. Filed separately (linked below).\n4. **#303** (chamfer/deburr) is not fixed by this. It needs the operation's own edge break to count as intended.",
